# GitHub language bar mechanics (verified against Linguist behavior):
#   The bar only shows languages registered in github/linguist. CatBase is NOT
#   registered; registration needs an upstream PR plus real-world usage
#   (CONTRIBUTING.md asks for ~2000 files on GitHub per extension — a search
#   today finds 2 .catc files in the world). So "CatBase" cannot appear in
#   the bar, and we do not pretend otherwise.
#
# What we CAN do honestly:
#   1. Map CatBase source to the registered language it most resembles.
#      CatBase syntax is Python-flavored (def/print/str/int, # comments),
#      so .catc/.cat are counted as Python via linguist-language.
#   2. Mark logs and generated files linguist-generated so they leave the stats.
#   3. Mark our install scripts + binaries linguist-vendored (they are delivery
#      artifacts, not the project's source) so Shell stops dominating the bar.
#   Result (verified via gh api after push): the bar reflects the actual
#   product — the CatBase package manager source — instead of "100% Shell".

# --- CatBase source -> Python (closest registered language) ---
*.catc  linguist-language=Python
*.cat   linguist-language=Python

# --- logs / generated: excluded from stats ---
logs/*.log linguist-generated
*.diff     linguist-generated
*.lock     linguist-generated

# --- delivery artifacts: vendored (stay in repo, leave the stats) ---
install.sh     linguist-vendored
install.fish   linguist-vendored
scripts/**     linguist-vendored
probe/**       linguist-vendored
catpm/catpm52  linguist-vendored
catpm/catpm5   linguist-vendored
catpm/catpm4   linguist-vendored
catpm/catpm3   linguist-vendored
catpm/catpm2   linguist-vendored
demo*/**       linguist-vendored

# --- source-probe tool: bash entry points are delivery artifacts ---
tools/srcprobe/probe             linguist-vendored
tools/srcprobe/catpm-probe       linguist-vendored
tools/srcprobe/catpm-quickstart  linguist-vendored
